    <briefdescription>
<para>Detects and classifies deterministic edge-case conditions in the updates state machine. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>All public methods are thread-safe. The handler maintains no persistent mutable state beyond the <computeroutput><ref refid="structthemis_1_1updates_1_1_edge_case_stats" kindref="compound">EdgeCaseStats</ref></computeroutput> counters.</para>
<para>Detection priority order (highest to lowest):<orderedlist>
<listitem><para>STATE_FAILED_LOCKED (7402)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>STATE_ALREADY_IN_PROGRESS (7401)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>STATE_TRANSITION_TIMEOUT (7403)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>ROLLBACK_CASCADE_DETECTED (7423)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>ROLLBACK_ISOLATION_ACTIVE (7426)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>ROLLBACK_PARTIAL_SUCCESS (7424)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>PATCH_APPLY_FAILED (7440)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>NETWORK_PARTITION (7460)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>COORDINATION_ORDERING_VIOLATION (7464) </para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
